{"case":{"approved_prefix":"django/","command":["python","/verification/verify.py"],"entry_files":["django/contrib/auth/validators.py"],"entry_lines":{"django/contrib/auth/validators.py":1},"id":"django__django-11099","image":"sha256:df8f0ef9be4fb1f710c20ba9738a4ec6fa68d2a1d6422fce277cbfc4b69ed73e","issue":"UsernameValidator allows trailing newline in usernames\nDescription\n\t\nASCIIUsernameValidator and UnicodeUsernameValidator use the regex \nr'^[\\w.@+-]+$'\nThe intent is to only allow alphanumeric characters as well as ., @, +, and -. However, a little known quirk of Python regexes is that $ will also match a trailing newline. Therefore, the user name validators will accept usernames which end with a newline. You can avoid this behavior by instead using \\A and \\Z to terminate regexes. For example, the validator regex could be changed to\nr'\\A[\\w.@+-]+\\Z'\nin order to reject usernames that end with a newline.\nI am not sure how to officially post a patch, but the required change is trivial - using the regex above in the two validators in contrib.auth.validators.\n","issue_url":"https://github.com/django/django/pull/11099","provenance":"Build004 curated SWE-bench Verified case; human-localized entry files. Public training contamination possible. Entry files and line windows derive from historical maintainer localization; reference text is not supplied to the model.","qualified":true,"reference_digest":"cf203df5a90df3747f2d9a59cb0d02620d70228c29cb0c3477e5509056c19c09","repository":"django/django","revision":"d26b2424437dabeeca94d7900b37d2df4410da0c","source_digest":"400bd3f7a447f2fd328eee79ef9cffb7376335dfcdf80fe5c5ebcd5120c65df1","source_url":"https://github.com/django/django/tree/d26b2424437dabeeca94d7900b37d2df4410da0c","split":"evaluation","title":"UsernameValidator allows trailing newline in usernames","verification_digest":"63fe256a5ca0c6cd0b93de5eb127652f50184c868a615841dba8493441c31014"},"registry_version":"repository-cases-v1"}